## Trust over cost (D-34 — Dan 2026-07-12, authoritative purpose statement)

**The end goal of model routing is trusted output, not saved money.** A cheap model whose output cannot be trusted is pointless to use; a cheap model **paired with a verifier that reaches genuine agreement** is the product. Cost is the constraint; trust is the goal.

- **D-65:** Narrowing **when** a verifier lane fires does **not** weaken agreement/fix-closure **when** that lane fires. Trigger trim ≠ cost-first.
- **Default pattern (when a verifier lane is triggered):** cheapest appropriate worker → that lane's verifier → peer deliberate until agree (D-30/D-33) → orchestrator presents. Do **not** invent extra Grok lanes for ceremony.
- **Tier table = trust calibration, not a price list:** escalation (2-fail, stall-advisor, Sonnet diagnose, Fable) exists for when agreement cannot be reached at the cheap tier.
- **D-65 / D-36 skips:** routine T0/T1 with obvious approach + green mechanical tests may skip Solution/Build/UI-PW/Ship per § Risk-based routing — not a license to skip PROTECTED Sonnet or D-51/D-42 on visible UI. The **≥97% conf floor** (D-47) is separate and is **not** waived; do **not** dispatch premium models solely to raise a confidence number.
- **No unverified cheap output reaches Dan** on any lane where a verifier trigger fired: missing evidence line = NOT RUN.
- Parity automatic per D-32.

## Platform parity (D-20 — all Composer sessions)

`.cursor/rules/*` **alwaysApply** rules bind **every** Composer session — desktop IDE (Windows PC), mobile Cursor app, and cloud VM — with **identical** harness behavior: ship-loop tiers (`ship-loop.mdc`), repair loop (§ Repair loop), planning verify loop (§ Planning verify loop), Q&A verify loop (§ Q&A verify loop), verification ladder (§ Verification ladder), security gate (`security-review-gate.mdc`), stall-advisor (D-19), Ship/Critical/Work/Planning/Q&A/Solution/Build-Checker/**UI-Playwright** verifiers (§ Solution deliberation, D-36/D-43/D-45), **UI before/after screenshots (D-51, `ui-before-after.mdc`)**, evidence lines, and fix-closure. Cloud agents read the same rules from the repo; **no "mobile-lite" orchestration**.

Mechanical evidence gate identical across clients — CI gate-check on PRs; local pre-push hook auto-installed by npm `prepare` blocks high-risk direct-to-main pushes without commit-message evidence (D-28/D-29).

**Exceptions** — mobile/cloud differ **only** where physically impossible (e.g. Dan must tap secrets in Cursor Environments UI; branch-only ship when the prompt forbids `main` push). Document exceptions in `AGENTS.md` and `docs/cloud-agent-iphone-setup.md`, not in separate rule files.

**Environment auto-detection (D-35 — Dan 2026-07-13):** agents determine their execution environment **mechanically, never from Dan's words** — two environment **classes**: **local checkout** (win32 / non-`/workspace` path — currently `C:\Projects\stageverify`, includes any future dev machine; local secrets) and **cloud VM** (`/workspace`, linux, cloud-injected AGENTS.md instructions, Environments-UI secrets). The phone is a viewport onto cloud agents, not a third environment class. Dan NEVER needs to say "I'm on my phone/mobile" — such statements are ergonomic context only (short replies, tappable links, QR codes) and MUST NOT be used as routing, tier, ship-workflow, or rule triggers. Environment-dependent behavior (branch+PR default vs full local ship loop, secrets availability, hook installation) keys off the detected environment; task-class triggers (e.g. D-27 phone-first product surfaces) key off what is being built, never which device Dan is holding.

**Parity by default (D-32 — Dan 2026-07-12):** every **new** rule, gate, loop, script, or workflow is platform-parity **by default** — it binds desktop Windows PC, mobile Cursor, and cloud VM identically the moment it is created. New rules do NOT need a per-rule "Platform parity" clause (existing clauses stay as documentation, not opt-ins); enforcement mechanics must be client-neutral (node scripts via `path.join` + `readText()` CRLF-normalize; hooks via npm `prepare`; CI on PRs). Mobile parity means alwaysApply rules + cloud-VM execution mechanics — the phone itself runs no local git or hooks. The only thing a new rule may declare is an **exception**, and only when physically impossible on a client — documented in `AGENTS.md` and `docs/cloud-agent-iphone-setup.md`, never silently assumed. A rule that works on one client and not the others is a bug, not a variant.

## 2-fail + 3-fail stuck ladder (Dan 2026-07-03; D-19 stall; D-50 third-fail Agree + Grok implement; **D-55** third try = D-50)

**Default implementer:** **Composer** for non-UI and **simple UI** (D-65); **Sol** (Task→`gpt-5.6-sol-high` directly) for **visual-judgment UI** only; **orchestrator** (D-92) completes the ship loop. **Exception:** after **D-50 stuck-task Agree** on the **3rd try**, **Grok implements** that stuck scope only until that ship closes — then Sol resumes for visual-judgment UI; Composer otherwise.

**D-55 (hard rule — Dan 2026-07-25):** After **2 consecutive fails** on the **same task/ship scope** (session or continued thread), the **next attempt (3rd try) is automatic D-50** — **not** another Composer-only implement+verify retry, **not** a 3rd Ship Verifier retrospective close, **not** another build/Playwright/verify-fix loop without **D-50 Phase A Agree** first. **Fail type and fingerprint do not exempt the 3rd try** from D-50 (fingerprint still governs **2nd-fail** handling only — stall-advisor vs Sonnet diagnose — below).

On the **2nd consecutive fail** on the same scope:

- **Same failure fingerprint as 1st** → **Grok stall-advisor** (mandatory; § below) — hypotheses feed **D-50 Agree**; **no** Composer-only “attempt 3” after stall-advisor.
- **Different fingerprint** → **Sonnet 5** diagnose-only (root cause, hypothesis) — feeds **D-50 Agree**; **no** Composer-only “attempt 3” after diagnose.

- Sonnet (pre-D-50) = **diagnostic / Agree peer** — no commits, no file edits, no ship loop except as **stuck-task Agree** participant (D-50).
- Grok stall-advisor = **advisory only** — hypotheses + next experiments; no commits, no file edits, no ship loop.

**Counting failures (consecutive on same scope):** any failed **implement+verify** cycle (`npm run build`, `verify:*` / Playwright, local UI Playwright fix loops), **Ship Verifier FAIL** (including after incomplete fix-closure re-verify), and equivalent stuck-ship validation failures on the **same task/ship scope**. Security-gate Sonnet runs are separate — not counted. **Two consecutive counted fails → 3rd try = D-50 automatically** — Dan does not need to say "escalate." Fingerprint match is **not** required to trigger D-50 on the 3rd try (**D-55**). **D-54:** Ship Verifier evidence-gap closes follow the same consecutive-fail counter — **no 4th** retrospective Ship Verifier close on the same scope without **D-50 Agree** completed.

### Same failure fingerprint (D-19)

Two consecutive fails on the same task scope share a fingerprint when the **normalized failure key** matches:

| Source | Fingerprint key |
|--------|-----------------|
| `verify:*` / `scripts/verify-*.mjs` | script name (or npm script) + first failed assertion or error message (whitespace-normalized; strip timestamps/paths that drift per run) |
| `npm run build` / `tsc` | error code + file + line (e.g. `TS2322:src/foo.ts:42`) |
| Playwright / runtime | test or step name + error class + stable message substring (first 120 chars, normalized) |
| Ship Verifier (Grok post-push) | `ship-verifier` + finding class — for mandatory **evidence gaps** use `ship-verifier + missing:<token>` where `<token>` is one of `ui-readability`, `ui-playwright`, `build-checker`, `ui-before-after`, `security-gate`, `solution-verifier`, `sonnet-instruct`, `high-risk-adversarial`, `sonnet-verify` (include all missing tokens, **sorted**); optional suffix `+commits:<short-range>` when the same ship scope spans multiple pushes in one conversation; whitespace-normalized; strip drifting paths/timestamps/task-ids from the key |

**Different fingerprint** on 2nd fail → skip Grok stall-advisor; **Sonnet diagnose-only** on 2nd fail (implement+verify path) — **2nd fail always counts** toward D-55. Ship Verifier: **2nd same fingerprint** → mandatory stall-advisor (**D-54**); **2nd different fingerprint** still counts as the 2nd consecutive fail; **3rd try** on scope = **D-50** regardless of fingerprint (**D-55**).

### Failure sequence (ordered)

1. **1st fail** → Composer retry (+ optional self-trace per `MODEL_DOSSIER.md` tag `composer-trace`) — this is **attempt 2**.
2. **2nd consecutive fail** on same scope → **2nd-fail lane only** (counts toward D-55): **same fingerprint** → **Grok stall-advisor** (mandatory); **different fingerprint** → **Sonnet 5** diagnose-only. **Do not** start another ordinary Composer implement+verify / Ship Verifier close / verify-fix as the “3rd try.”
3. **3rd try (automatic D-55 + D-50)** → **D-50 stuck-task escalation** (§ below) — **mandatory** after two consecutive fails: **Grok ↔ Sonnet 5** peer deliberation until **Agree** on root cause + exact fix plan (Solution-style Agree + D-30/D-33; incorporate stall-advisor / Sonnet diagnose output); if scope touches CF/rules/auth, Sonnet uses **diagnose/Agree** role (security gate slug per `security-review-gate.mdc` when high-risk — separate mandatory gate before push unchanged) → **Grok implements** agreed fix for that scope only → normal D-43 verify ladder (UI Playwright / Build Checker when triggered; **orchestrator only** commit + push + deploy — implementer workers never ship; Ship Verifier; Sonnet security gate before push if high-risk) → **Sol (UI-class) / Composer (non-UI) resumes** default implementer for the next task.
4. **Sonnet diagnose-only without two prior consecutive fails** — when **only one** fail so far and ANY of: `confStart < 70`; Dan says "still broken" without new hypothesis (after 1st-fail self-trace); architecture unclear after one Composer pass. Composer implements after Sonnet returns — **not** a substitute for step 3 when two consecutive fails already occurred (**D-55** blocks ordinary attempt 3).

Other Sonnet triggers: security verifier before push; architecture unclear after synthesis. **Not** for scouts or routine T0/T1/T2 before 1st fail + retry. Opus 4.6 = locked fallback only if Sonnet security gate returns HIGH Composer cannot resolve.

## 3-fail stuck-task escalation (D-50 — Dan 2026-07-24; **3rd try mandatory D-55**)

**Trigger:** **Two consecutive fails** on the **same task/ship scope** → the **next attempt (3rd try) is automatic D-50** (**D-55**): any mix of implement+verify, `npm run build`, Playwright/`verify:*`, and Ship Verifier FAILs counts; **fingerprint match not required** for D-50 on the 3rd try. Includes post–stall-advisor and post–Sonnet-diagnose on the 2nd fail — those lanes do **not** authorize a Composer-only 3rd attempt. **Automatic** — not gated on Dan saying "escalate."

**Phase A — Agree (readonly Tasks):** Orchestrator (usually Composer) synthesizes failure history + fingerprints → dispatch **Grok** (`cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast`, `generalPurpose`, `readonly`) and **Sonnet 5** (`claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` per D-38 allowlist; on rejection retry next allowlist slug, `generalPurpose` or `security-review` when CF/rules/auth in scope — **diagnose/Agree only**, not implementation) → peer deliberate until **Agree** on root cause + **exact fix plan** (file paths, acceptance = named `verify:*` PASS). Max 3 Agree cycles; unresolved → present both positions to Dan. **Evidence:** `stuck-task-agree: <grok-task-id> + <sonnet-task-id>` + model lines + verdict **Agree** (or `escalated to Dan`).

**Phase B — Implement (Grok carve-out):** **Grok** (Task `generalPurpose`, `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` or orchestrating Grok parent **only for this stuck scope**) writes product code per agreed plan — **overrides D-43/D-37 Composer-only implementer lock for this stuck task only**. Grok-as-implementer **never** commits, pushes, or deploys (orchestrator owns ship). **Evidence:** `stuck-implementer: grok (<task-id or inline session>)` + `implementer-exception: D-50 stuck scope`.

**Phase C — Close stuck ship:** Run normal post-implement ladder on the agreed diff. **High-risk/T3 stuck ships:** close via **D-60 Phases 3–5** (`high-risk-adversarial:` → `sonnet-verify:` → D-38) — do **not** substitute Build Checker / UI Playwright as if D-60 were absent. Non-high-risk: UI Playwright when visible UI; Build Checker when judgment needed; **orchestrator** commit + push + deploy (implementer workers never ship); Sonnet **security gate** before push when high-risk; Ship Verifier after push. Stuck-task ship **done** → **Sol (UI-class) / Composer (non-UI)** is default implementer again for new work (D-43 lock restored).

**D-62 — Post-D-50 retry rounds (Dan 2026-08-05):** If after a completed **D-50 Phase A Agree → Phase B Grok implement** the **same task/ship scope** still fails under the same counted-fail classes as D-50 (implement+verify / build / Playwright / Ship Verifier — security-gate runs excluded), do **not** resume Composer-only implement+verify and do **not** open unbounded retries. Allow at most **2 additional retry rounds**, each = full **Phase A** (Grok↔Sonnet peer Agree on revised root cause + exact fix plan; Max 3 Agree peer iterations per round unchanged) → **Phase B** (Grok implements; still never commits/pushes/deploys) → Phase C ladder. **Grok remains stuck-scope implementer** across D-50 + D-62 rounds until ship closes or Dan escalate. Evidence each round: `stuck-task-agree: … (d62-round N/2)` + `stuck-implementer: grok …`. After **2** D-62 rounds still failing → **STOP** — escalate to Dan with clarifying questions (what's still broken, acceptance, scope); no 3rd D-62 round, no Composer spin. Amends D-50/D-55. Platform parity D-32.

**Platform parity:** D-32 — identical on desktop PC, mobile Cursor, cloud VM.

## Grok stall-advisor auto-invoke (Dan 2026-07-10 — D-19)

**Pain event:** Dan 2026-07-10 consecutive same-failure stall — Composer retried identical fixes without a cheap pivot.

Dispatch exactly **one** read-only Task when **2nd consecutive fail** on the same task/ship scope shares the **same failure fingerprint** as the 1st — from **implement+verify** **or** from **Ship Verifier FAIL** (D-54 evidence-gap class):

```text
Task({
  subagent_type: "generalPurpose",
  model: "cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast",
  readonly: true,
  description: "Stall advisor",
  prompt: "…symptom, fingerprint, task scope, files touched, prior fix attempts, self-trace block… Return hypotheses + ranked next experiments only — no implementation."
})
```

**Evidence:** completion report MUST include `stall-advisor: <task-id>` + `model: cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast`, or `stall-advisor: N/A (fingerprints differed)`. Missing Task id when trigger fired = **NOT RUN**.

**When NOT to invoke:** 1st fail only (including 1st Ship Verifier FAIL); 2nd fail with different fingerprint on implement+verify (→ Sonnet diagnose per § 2-fail); security-gate Sonnet; Repair Verifier on Dan repair intent; Planning Verifier on planning questions (§ Planning verify loop); Q&A Verifier on non-trivial Q&A (§ Q&A verify loop); Critical Reviewer pre-decision; Dan says skip. **One run per fingerprint per task/ship scope** — after **two consecutive fails**, **3rd try = D-50** § 3-fail (**D-55** — not a second stall-advisor; not another Composer-only retry; no 4th retrospective Ship Verifier close without Agree — **D-54**).

**vs Ship Verifier / Repair Verifier / Planning Verifier / Q&A Verifier / Critical Reviewer / high-risk-adversarial:** orthogonal roles — Ship Verifier = post-ship scope check (its **same-fingerprint FAIL ladder** feeds § 2-fail/D-50 per D-54, distinct Task from stall-advisor); Repair Verifier = Dan repair-intent pre-close (§ Repair loop); Planning Verifier = pre-present planning accuracy (§ Planning verify loop); Q&A Verifier = pre-present Q&A accuracy (§ Q&A verify loop); Critical Reviewer = pre-finalize harness/architecture decisions; **`high-risk-adversarial:`** = D-60 Phase 3 product T3 diff review (`high-risk-sonnet-loop.mdc`); stall-advisor = mid-task same-failure pivot. Same model slug; never satisfy repair + ship + stall + Critical Reviewer + high-risk-adversarial with one Task unless explicitly same scope/event.

## Security gate

Invocation, model lock, and evidence requirements: **`security-review-gate.mdc`** (sole authoritative copy). Run **before push** — not after commit. Never self-report PASS from Composer inline review.

## Task model start failures (Couldn't start)

UI **"New subagent → Couldn't start"**, Task **"Invalid model selection"**, or **"Model could not be resolved"** = **platform rejection of that slug** — not a soft skip. Immediately retry with the next allowlisted slug for that lane (`fallback-from:`). Grok verifier/stall/ship/planning/Q&A Tasks use **`cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` only** (do not dispatch `grok-4.5-fast-xhigh`). Security gate preference: **`claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` first** per `security-review-gate.mdc` (D-38 allowlist). Do not halt the verify/ship loop on the first failed start when another allowlisted slug remains.

## Post-change model audit

After every substantive code/config change, brief audit before reporting done.

**Low-risk exemption:** read-only audits, docs/rules-only → short line OK (e.g. `Model routing: T0 docs/rules; no escalation`).

**Code/config** — compact block:

```
### Model audit
| Change | Archetype | Tier | Worker | Scouts parallel? | Escalation review? | Verdict |
```

When security gate triggered: `security-gate-id: <uuid>`, `model: <Sonnet gate slug per security-review-gate.mdc D-38 allowlist>`, `actual model invocation evidence: yes/no/unknown`, `verdict: PASS|MEDIUM|HIGH|NOT RUN`. No UUID → **NOT RUN**, not PASS.

Complete ship loop (`ship-loop.mdc`) before declaring done for code/config changes.

